1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,586
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:08,508
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,677
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,310
[Ibyang] <i>Am I really your child?</i>

7
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:22,272
[Olga] <i>You just got scolded!</i>
<i>You're sulking already?</i>

8
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,357
[Karla] <i>There, they're the ones</i>
<i>we're chasing.</i>

9
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,942
And that suitcase?

10
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,528
It contains five million pesos,
which we need to get.

11
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,905
- [Ame, in English] <i>I have a bright idea.</i>
- [Karla] <i>Where's your friend?</i>

12
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:33,825
<i>- Didn't you say you're with your friend?</i>
<i>- Sweetheart, you're the only one I love.</i>

13
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:34,993
[Gavin] <i>That's just my friend.</i>

14
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,536
[in English] That's Gavin!

15
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,954
Who will you choose?

16
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,956
Your best friend or your girlfriend?

17
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,207
[Cathy, in English] <i>What's going on here?</i>

18
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,334
- [Boyet] <i>You're causing trouble!</i>
- [Cathy's mom] Stop it!

19
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:44,377
[in English] That's my daughter!

20
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,545
Let me go!

21
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:46,838
- [Cathy's mom, in English] <i>Call security!</i>
- [Gavin] <i>Stay here.</i>

22
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:48,965
[Karla] <i>Gavin! Stop them!</i>

23
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:50,008
[Kiko] <i>Where's my money?</i>

24
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:52,302
- Boss, I really brought the five million.
- Hands up!

25
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:54,512
- I'm a cop!
- [cop] We'll take you to the station.

26
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:55,430
You'll explain there!

27
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:57,098
Oh, no, Atoy, she's just like you.

28
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,391
[Emerson] <i>Your sister is just as tough.</i>

29
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,476
Why? Are they siblings?

30
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:00,643
[hushes]

31
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:04,647
[Ame] For the success
of Operation Suitcase!

32
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:07,233
- [all, in English] Cheers!
- [in English] Hey, cheers! Cheers, cheers!

33
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,235
- [in English] I have to go.
- Audrey, wait.

34
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:10,403
[Atoy on the phone] <i>I still love you.</i>

35
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:11,613
Audrey.

36
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:14,949
I really miss you and Tatoy, Sister Ame.

37
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,910
Hey, Ibyang, what happened?

38
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,828
What are the plans for the child?

39
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,288
Do what we agreed on.

40
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:22,165
That's your only job. Okay?

41
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:23,708
[Olga] <i>Hello. Friend?</i>

42
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,835
<i>I thought of something</i>
<i>we could make money from.</i>

43
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:26,753
PREVIOUSLY

44
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,046
<i>This is big money.</i>

45
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:29,964
[music ends]

46
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,424
[T-Bak] Oh, there.

47
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:32,842
- [Karla] Oh!
- [T-Bak] Oh, take it.

48
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:33,760
‪[grunts]

49
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:37,388
Hey. PJ texted me earlier.

50
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:39,933
He said Gavin and Jason want to join.

51
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,893
Oh, that's another bet! [smirks]

52
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:43,770
Gavin's coming?

53
00:01:43,853 --> 00:01:46,481
Oh? Why are you affected?

54
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,066
Oh, nothing!

55
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:50,401
Come on. Time out first. My God.

56
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,695
- [light music playing]
- [inhales]

57
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:55,448
[T-Bak] Gosh!

58
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:57,575
[man] My turn.

59
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:00,870
- [T-Bak] Oh.
- Oh, they're already here.

60
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:02,789
Wow. He's big.

61
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,124
He's big, huh.

62
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,500
- [music fades]
- So big.

63
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:07,961
Why isn't Gavin here?

64
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,796
[in English] He's with Cathy.

65
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:11,214
What? Let's go. Let's ball!

66
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:13,174
- [PJ] Game on, game on.
- [Jason] Oh.

67
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:15,051
[light music playing]

68
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:16,803
[T-Bak] Hey.

69
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,889
Don't be sad
just because Gavin isn't here.

70
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,016
[T-Bak] Don't worry.

71
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,810
He and Cathy will break up soon.

72
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:25,019
Hey. You…

73
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:27,272
We're Team Karla! Oh!

74
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:30,024
Shut up.

75
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,276
Keep dreaming, Karla.

76
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,903
[T-Bak] Game! The big one's mine.

77
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,155
There, oh!

78
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,656
[suave theme music playing]

79
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:38,575
[motorcycle revving]

80
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:39,534
[sewing machine whirring]

81
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:41,452
[scratches]

82
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:42,495
[snipping]

83
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,956
[clicking]

84
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,374
[sewing machine clacking]

85
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:48,418
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

86
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,461
[gunshots]

87
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:52,046
[clicking]

88
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:52,964
[clicking]

89
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:54,132
[snipping]

90
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:57,135
[music swells]

91
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:01,306
- [electronic blipping]
- [music fades]

92
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:03,641
[indistinct chattering]

93
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,143
One bag contains food.

94
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:06,603
The other contains clothes and a blanket.

95
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:07,770
Thank you very much.

96
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:10,648
I hope more people like you will help us.

97
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,566
[Cathy] You're welcome.

98
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:14,527
["In Nothing" instrumental music playing]

99
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,655
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Thank you.

100
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:21,993
Babe, are there more blankets there?

101
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:23,202
[in English] We might need more.

102
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:27,206
[in English] Babe?

103
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,875
♪ <i>It's not that…</i> ♪

104
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:30,168
[in English] Babe!

105
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,211
Gavin!

106
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,549
I've been calling you.

107
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,343
Why do you look spaced out?

108
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:42,013
Our companions might think

109
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:44,265
my boyfriend has no interest in helping.

110
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,892
I'll be embarrassed.

111
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:47,936
[in English] Sorry.

112
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:53,566
[pensive music playing]

113
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:57,987
Ma'am, this is expired.

114
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,156
Throw this away. It can't be used anymore.

115
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,658
Let me see.

116
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:07,038
Yes, it's expired.

117
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:15,296
But you know, they won't notice that.

118
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:18,424
Just cover it with a marker,
and let's just give it away.

119
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:19,592
But, ma'am--

120
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:23,972
These poor people,
they don't care if the food has mold.

121
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,848
Especially when they're hungry.

122
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:30,436
If they fail to read that it's expired,
then it's their fault.

123
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,147
What's important is we were able
to give a lot of items.

124
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,148
- [in English] Okay?
- Okay, ma'am.

125
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,108
[in English] No, it's not okay.

126
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,235
Gavin?

127
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:39,153
You know…

128
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,489
Bro, bro, dispose of that.

129
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:42,615
They might get sick.

130
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:46,411
They already lost their homes.
Don't add to their problems.

131
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:48,496
[in English] I can't believe
you'd do that, Cathy.

132
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:52,125
You would risk people's health,
just to look good on camera?

133
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,210
You're judging me too much.

134
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:55,920
If you were in my shoes,

135
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:58,840
what do you think you'd feel
if I did that?

136
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:00,967
[rousing music playing]

137
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:10,310
Ibyang!

138
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,645
Ibyang, get your bag!

139
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:15,440
[sneaky music playing]

140
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,108
Ibyang!

141
00:05:17,191 --> 00:05:18,609
[music fades]

142
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,278
- Oh!
- [Charmi] Oh, hello.

143
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,738
- I'll take care of that.
- Oh.

144
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,281
She already went upstairs.

145
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:26,159
She's so excited to be back here.

146
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,536
Where's Olga?

147
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:31,247
Wasn't she supposed to bring Ibyang here?

148
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:35,626
Ah, well, Olga has work now.

149
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:38,713
She had an early call time,

150
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:41,174
so she asked me instead.

151
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:45,887
Actually, she wanted to bring
the child to work,

152
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:49,474
but I said not to bring the child.
She might get tired.

153
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:52,977
Their taping is far. It's in Tanay.

154
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:55,354
Taping?

155
00:05:55,438 --> 00:05:58,232
What's she going to tape? Boxes?

156
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:00,068
[laughs] You're funny!

157
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:03,321
No. Olga is an actress.

158
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:05,782
Oh.

159
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:07,200
I knew it.

160
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:09,869
That's why she looked familiar.

161
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:13,581
I think I saw her in a TV series.

162
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,708
She was a patient there.

163
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:18,920
That's it. <i>Abot-Kamay na Pangarap</i>.

164
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:22,757
Yes, she was an extra there.
One of the extras who died.

165
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:23,841
[laughs]

166
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:25,009
Oh. Okay.

167
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:27,220
Her mom will pick her up.

168
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,555
I'll go ahead. I'm in a hurry.

169
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,557
[Charmi] All right. Mmm.

170
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:35,269
Ibyang, enjoy! I'll go ahead!

171
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:37,105
- Okay.
- I'll tell her. Okay.

172
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,022
Okay. Bye!

173
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,317
[sneaky music playing]

174
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,235
It's good.

175
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:44,070
- Hmm.
- Hey, Gavin!

176
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,279
Ice candy. Want some?

177
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:47,365
- Sure.
- Mmm.

178
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,034
[Putoy] Oh?

179
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,203
Just one? Take another!

180
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:53,454
For your girlfriend.

181
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:55,665
No, just one. It's okay. Thank you.

182
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:00,878
Did you see Karla?

183
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:04,173
Karla? Ah…

184
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,717
You know, she was looking for you earlier.

185
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:09,470
Didn't you see her?

186
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:12,723
And why are you looking for her?

187
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:15,726
Your girlfriend might get mad.

188
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:19,564
Because I want to talk to her about Cathy.

189
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:22,066
Oh!

190
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:23,651
["In Nothing" instrumental music playing]

191
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:25,153
Is that a lovers' quarrel?

192
00:07:26,904 --> 00:07:27,780
[in English] Something like that.

193
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:29,949
[clears throat]

194
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:32,702
Are you okay, bro?

195
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:35,496
We're just here.

196
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,331
We'll support you.

197
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,335
What's your problem?

198
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,922
[in English] I just realized…

199
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,592
I don't really know Cathy yet.

200
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:52,555
I thought she was okay, but I was wrong.

201
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:54,390
[in English] She's not
who I thought she is.

202
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,226
It's your fault!

203
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,521
From the start,
you should've gone for Karla instead!

204
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:01,439
[Billy] Exactly!

205
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:04,192
Kind, but brave.

206
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,818
Beautiful, but fierce!

207
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,528
And most of all…

208
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,946
[both] Not fake!

209
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:10,573
Hmm, exactly!

210
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:15,703
["In Nothing" by Wickermoss
with Neth Macam playing]

211
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:17,497
- [man 1] Let's share.
- [man 2] Unbelievable!

212
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:33,137
- Mmm!
- [mellow music playing]

213
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:38,267
Sister Karla, I know it's you.

214
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:40,645
I've missed you.

215
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:43,689
How did you know it was me?

216
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,900
That's impossible.

217
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:48,778
Well, I told her you were coming.

218
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,530
So, Karla?

219
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,533
Can you help me deliver that?

220
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:57,954
Because Atoy just told me now
that something needs to be delivered.

221
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:01,207
And I'm not even finished yet
with the other thing he asked me to do.

222
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:02,875
Okay, Sister Ame.

223
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:05,670
Just don't let Brother Atoy know
that I was the one who delivered it, okay?

224
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:09,840
Yes. Oh, thank you so much, Karla.

225
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,386
I'll come too, Sister Karla.

226
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:16,180
So we can bond.

227
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:18,099
Come on. Please?

228
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:19,225
This little one!

229
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:21,060
Bring her along,

230
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:23,563
so I can finish what I need to do.

231
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:26,566
Then when you get back,
I'll treat you with pares.

232
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:27,858
[Ibyang] Pares.

233
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:30,570
But what if her mom looks for her?

234
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,738
She'll be picked up tonight.

235
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:35,366
Her mom's working in Tanay.

236
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:36,617
Oh, Ibyang,

237
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,619
how are you and your mom?

238
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:39,704
Is she nice to you?

239
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:42,915
Yes. Mama is kind.

240
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:44,959
She takes care of me.

241
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:50,047
But she scolded me right away.

242
00:09:51,173 --> 00:09:53,426
Because I did something wrong.

243
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,052
What did you do?

244
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,470
[melancholic music playing]

245
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:58,431
Well, then…

246
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:01,434
I broke a lot of things.

247
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:06,230
I got scared because I thought
she didn't love me.

248
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:09,191
Hey. She loves you, I'm sure.

249
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:11,527
Not just because she scolded you,

250
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:12,862
she even looked for you.

251
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:16,407
You know, the fact that she came for you,

252
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:19,410
that's a sign she loves you.

253
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,704
Right?

254
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:25,583
[bright music playing]

255
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:27,918
[in English] Hi, Karla. Ibyang!

256
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:31,172
He suddenly came too.

257
00:10:31,255 --> 00:10:32,465
[Ibyang chuckles]

258
00:10:32,548 --> 00:10:37,762
- Maybe he loves you too! [giggling]
- Shh! Hey! He might hear you.

259
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:40,056
[Karla] Ibyang.

260
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:44,935
Where are you going? I'll take you.

261
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:50,483
- No.
- We have… We have a ride!

262
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:53,527
No need. Ibyang and I can do this.

263
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:55,071
We can do this, right?

264
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,698
I insist. Let's go.

265
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,450
Oh, let's go, Ibyang. Sit in the back.

266
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:00,910
[in English] Okay. [giggling]

267
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:03,537
I'll just put this here, okay?

268
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,997
[Ibyang] Yes.

269
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:07,875
[Gavin sighs]

270
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:10,252
[music fades]

271
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:13,130
You're coming with us. Are you sure?

272
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,216
Won't Cathy get mad at you?

273
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:17,301
Don't worry about that.

274
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,136
[in English] So, where are we going?

275
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,597
[bright music playing]

276
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,224
I can handle this.

277
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:35,528
[Karla] Brother Emerson,

278
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:37,530
I already delivered what Sister Ame
asked me to deliver.

279
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:38,447
We're on our way home.

280
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:42,201
[indistinct chattering]

281
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:47,706
Really?

282
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,291
Fine.

283
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,543
Hurry up, okay.

284
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:51,961
[pleasant music playing]

285
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:53,129
[Gavin] Let's just wait there.

286
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:56,257
Do you want snacks or coffee? My treat.

287
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,175
Can we have both?

288
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:00,803
- [in English] Sure.
- Hey, Ibyang, we're not like that.

289
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:02,430
Gavin, that was just a joke.

290
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:06,016
But it's up to you if you want
to take it seriously.

291
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:13,941
Wait a minute. Can I quickly pee?

292
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:15,734
Oh, wow!

293
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:18,404
[in English] Mamsh, I love this look!

294
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:20,823
[in English] It's like, you know,
giving very quiet luxury,

295
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:23,075
with arrogance and horns.

296
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:25,244
- [chuckles]
- [giggles]

297
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:26,162
Charmi.

298
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:27,246
Yes?

299
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:29,248
[in English] Can you please
call my manager?

300
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:32,668
[in English] And order me
a blueberry cheesecake without cheese.

301
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:35,629
- A blueberry cheesecake without--
- A blueberry cheesecake without cheese?!

302
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:37,548
[laughing]

303
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:40,468
What?! [laughs]

304
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,720
- Okay. I'll go with you.
- [sneaky music playing]

305
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:44,972
- We'll just follow to the coffee shop.
- Okay, fine.

306
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:48,767
[laughing]

307
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,770
Hey, let's get serious now.
Enough of that.

308
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:54,648
- Actor's in now.
- Hey, actor's in.

309
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,859
[deep breathing]

310
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,235
[indistinct]

311
00:12:58,319 --> 00:12:59,820
That's my mom.

312
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:03,699
- What?
- That's my mom.

313
00:13:06,535 --> 00:13:10,664
If this gig becomes successful,
we'll be loaded.

314
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,625
I'll check out my cart right away,
shopping time!

315
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:15,211
Buy everything you want!

316
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:18,005
A hundred thousand is nothing
compared to what we'll earn now.

317
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:20,508
[cackling]

318
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:21,800
Oh, come on. Let's go to the coffee shop.

319
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,887
- Let's go, hurry!
- One hundred thousand, come to mama!

320
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,180
[cackles]

321
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,975
Oh, oh. Sorry-- Sorry, sir.

322
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,393
- [Ibyang] Sorry, sir.
- [Karla] ibyang!

323
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,436
[Ibyang] That's my mom!

324
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,812
[tense music playing]

325
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,523
[Ibyang] Where's my mom?

326
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,609
- Huh?
- [Karla] Where?

327
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:41,278
She was just here earlier.

328
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,405
Where is she?

329
00:13:44,114 --> 00:13:45,491
She's in Tanay, right?

330
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:46,825
Isn't that where her taping is?

331
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:52,248
[in English] Oh, I'm sorry
to keep you waiting.

332
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:53,958
- [in English] No problem.
- [in English] I'm sorry.

333
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:55,084
Oh!

334
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,088
- [in English] You may take your seat.
- [in English] Why, thank you, kind sir.

335
00:14:00,297 --> 00:14:03,050
[sneaky music playing]

336
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:07,179
- [in English] Um, are you British?
- [clears throat]

337
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:09,098
[in English] Um, oh, no.

338
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:10,599
[in English] I'm from Caloocan.

339
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:14,770
[in English] Um,
I just travel there a lot.

340
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:15,980
[chuckles]

341
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,106
[in English] I love Europe.

342
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,440
[in English] Really?

343
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:21,569
- I also came from there last week.
- [Olga] Oh!

344
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:23,612
[in English] When was
the last time you went there?

345
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:25,114
[in English] Ah, where did you stay?

346
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:26,699
[chuckles]

347
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:30,244
- [phone ringing]
- [in English] Oh, excuse me.

348
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:32,621
- [in English] Oh, it's my daughter.
- Oh.

349
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:34,707
[Olga on the phone] <i>Hi!</i>

350
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:38,252
[in English] <i>Oh, hello,</i>
<i>my beautiful daughter.</i>

351
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,630
Mama, is that you?

352
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,008
[in English] Of course, my darling.

353
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:45,009
[chuckles]

354
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:47,386
[in English] I'm quite busy right now.

355
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:50,389
[in English] Oh, okay. I'll call you back.

356
00:14:50,472 --> 00:14:51,682
[in English] Ta-ta!

357
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,559
[in English] "Ta-ta"?

358
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,979
Why does Mama talk like that?

359
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:59,315
Isn't she at a taping?

360
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:01,025
Maybe she's just in character.

361
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:05,571
[in English] I ordered for us.

362
00:15:05,654 --> 00:15:09,116
- [music fades]
- [in English] Wow!

363
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:11,535
For you.

364
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:12,995
[in English] Wow.

365
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:15,581
[light music playing]

366
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:18,042
- Thank you, brother!
- Of course.

367
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:20,878
Oh no! I'm embarrassed.

368
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:23,589
You already came with us,
and now you're treating us to coffee.

369
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:24,965
It's fine.

370
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,550
Caramel macchiato for us.

371
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:29,720
[in English] For Ibyang, milk chocolate.

372
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:33,057
Ibyang, maybe you want something to eat?
Just tell me.

373
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,517
There are delicious pastries outside.

374
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:36,644
Check them out.

375
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:38,228
Really?

376
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,480
Of course.

377
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,775
You'll pay for it?

378
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:44,860
Of course. Just choose.

379
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,195
I'll take care of it.

380
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:51,617
[music fades]

381
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:55,287
Gavin, won't Cathy look for you?

382
00:15:55,871 --> 00:15:57,915
Did you tell her you're coming with us?

383
00:15:58,499 --> 00:15:59,917
[in English] I don't need to do that.

384
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,669
[in English] She's not my mom.

385
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:03,671
Did you fight?

386
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:05,714
Not really.

387
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,759
I just got tired of being with her.

388
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:12,262
Because I'm just her assistant
when she does volunteer work.

389
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:15,349
Or if not, just the videographer.

390
00:16:15,432 --> 00:16:19,186
Gosh! If the videographer and assistant
were as handsome as you,

391
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:20,521
I'd be happy.

392
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,398
Let me see, let me see!

393
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:23,899
Oh!

394
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,777
[in English] That's my boy
from Barangay Tabang Lupa!

395
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,696
There, oh. Cute dimple, oh.

396
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:30,656
Stop teasing me.

397
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,449
Me, handsome?

398
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:35,369
No, ugly.

399
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:37,538
Do you like that?

400
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:39,832
[light music playing]

401
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:42,793
You know, love your face.

402
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:46,630
Because no one else made that,
except you and your mom.

403
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:48,340
[music fades]

404
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:49,258
[in English] Legit!

405
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:51,719
[light music playing]

406
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:54,930
You know, Karla, I like being with you.

407
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:56,974
[in English] Why I didn't see that before?

408
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,309
Why did you say that all of a sudden?

409
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:02,062
Because you're genuine.

410
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:04,565
[in English] I can be
my true self when I'm with you.

411
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:08,569
Why? With Cathy, not so?

412
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:12,614
To be honest, no.

413
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:15,242
Because even she isn't real.

414
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:18,746
I didn't realize right away
that she was just pretending.

415
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:21,540
[pensive music playing]

416
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,265
[in English] Why are you selling it?

417
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,267
What a waste.

418
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:41,643
[in English] No.

419
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,104
[in English] Not to me.

420
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:46,190
- [chuckles softly]
- [sneaky music playing]

421
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:49,610
Um, my ex left that after…

422
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:52,196
after he…

423
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:54,823
dumped me for another woman.

424
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,745
He wanted it back,

425
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:02,414
because it's limited edition.

426
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:03,332
[man] Oh.

427
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,250
[in English] But I don't care.

428
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:07,086
[in English] I just want my revenge.

429
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,796
[in English] Serves him right.

430
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:11,632
But maybe

431
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:14,760
you can give me a discount?

432
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,513
[in English] Maybe
you can drop the price to…

433
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:19,640
150k?

434
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:22,184
[in English] You want
to get rid of this, right?

435
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:25,646
[in English] Oh.

436
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:26,688
[music fades]

437
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:27,856
[in English] Excuse me.

438
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,983
[in English] I'm so sorry.
I can't help it, but…

439
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:35,864
Um, my husband
is a watch collector, and um…

440
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:39,034
it's our anniversary.

441
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,203
[in English] Sir, can I see that?

442
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:42,371
[in English] Ah, sure.

443
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:43,664
[Charmi, in English] Thank you.

444
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:48,544
[in English] Oh my God!

445
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:50,379
Is this it?

446
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:51,839
[in English] In the flesh!

447
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:52,798
[chuckles]

448
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:53,966
[gasps]

449
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,801
[in English] Oh my God!

450
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:57,427
[sneaky music playing]

451
00:18:57,511 --> 00:19:01,140
This is one of the collections
my husband is looking for.

452
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,641
[in English] This is very rare!

453
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:04,143
Only four exist.

454
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:05,936
- [in English] Yes.
- Three are in museums.

455
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:07,396
[in English] Oh God!

456
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,731
[in English] Oh, love it! Oh.

457
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,401
- [chuckles]
- [Charmi] Oh, um…

458
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:16,655
Um, how much are you selling this for?

459
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,366
- [in English] Two hundred.
- [in English] Deal.

460
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:20,576
- [in English] Oh, s-sorry.
- Hmm?

461
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,202
[in English] It's already sold.

462
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,538
What? Really?

463
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:27,499
- You'll buy it? Two hundred?
- [man] Yes.

464
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,251
Can you afford it?

465
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,420
- [man] Mm-hmm.
- You're sure?

466
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:33,297
- [in English] Sure.
- Oh.

467
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:35,883
[Charmi] Too bad.

468
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,551
That would've been perfect for my husband.

469
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:41,180
[in English] Well,
you are a very lucky customer.

470
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:43,765
Very. Thank you!

471
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:48,395
[scoffs]

472
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:50,856
[in English] How much again?

473
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:52,316
[in English] Two hundred.

474
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:54,151
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

475
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:07,080
[Mercado, in English]
<i>The laptop is locked and requires a code.</i>

476
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:10,751
<i>Aside from the ambassador,</i>
<i>the only person who knows the code</i>

477
00:20:10,834 --> 00:20:13,545
<i>is the head of IT of the embassy.</i>

478
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:14,796
<i>She is Lily Santiago.</i>

479
00:20:15,797 --> 00:20:18,217
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

480
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,594
[Mercado] <i>After your retrieval</i>
<i>at the embassy,</i>

481
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:21,887
<i>she went into hiding.</i>

482
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:23,764
<i>And according to our intel,</i>

483
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:27,059
<i>she is the goddaughter</i>
<i>of the mayor of San Lazaro City,</i>

484
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:30,729
<i>and there's a big possibility</i>
<i>she's hiding here.</i>

485
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,565
<i>Your mission is to get her,</i>

486
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:36,068
<i>not just to decode the laptop,</i>

487
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:39,321
<i>but to save her life</i>
<i>because there's a big possibility</i>

488
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:42,282
<i>the Zahran embassy</i>
<i>is also looking for her.</i>

489
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,161
[in English] <i>Good luck, Padua.</i>

490
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:52,709
[music fades]

491
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:59,508
[gate hinge squeaks]

492
00:20:59,591 --> 00:21:00,968
Thanks to the boss.

493
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:02,552
Chief, thank you.

494
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:03,553
[group member 1] We're leaving now.

495
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:06,390
The Mayor is so kind.
I am completely satisfied.

496
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:11,353
Let's go.

497
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:22,322
[gate hinge squeaks]

498
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:23,282
[music fades]

499
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:24,825
- Oh, sir.
- [Atoy] Sir.

500
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:30,122
Is the Mayor there? Can I talk to him?

501
00:21:30,205 --> 00:21:31,373
Don't you have an appointment scheduled?

502
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:35,544
No, really.

503
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:39,631
Just go to the municipal hall
so someone can assist you.

504
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:45,721
I really want to talk to the Mayor.

505
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:52,185
Sorry, sir. We're strict right now
because the Mayor received a death threat.

506
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,186
[Atoy] Oh.

507
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,190
- Okay, sir.
- Okay, sir. Sorry.

508
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:01,028
[music swells]

509
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:14,333
[in English] Oh, I'll… I'll go ahead.

510
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:16,084
- [in English] Thank you.
- [man, in English] Thank you.

511
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,377
[in English] Thank you.

512
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:18,962
[chuckles]

513
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:20,130
[in English] Okay.

514
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,466
[in English] Bye. Enjoy!

515
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,343
[chuckles]

516
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,763
[sneaky music playing]

517
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,072
[in English] Oh my…

518
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,325
[in English] Oh, it's fake!

519
00:22:48,408 --> 00:22:49,993
[in English] I got scammed!

520
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,369
[in English] Scammer!

521
00:22:52,245 --> 00:22:55,624
[tense music playing]

522
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:00,879
[in English] Mama?

523
00:23:02,297 --> 00:23:04,966
[man, in English] Stop her! Get that girl!

524
00:23:05,675 --> 00:23:07,969
[in English] Get that girl! Scammer!

525
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,600
Sister Karla!

526
00:23:14,101 --> 00:23:15,727
I saw Mama!

527
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,104
[in English] Are you sure?

528
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:18,980
Yes.

529
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,149
I thought she was

530
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:22,692
at the taping.

531
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:25,362
But Mama was just pretending!

532
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:29,449
Didn't Sister Ame say that Brother Atoy
and your mama know each other?

533
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,369
Maybe they just have the same job.

534
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:33,870
No.

535
00:23:34,412 --> 00:23:37,666
It looked like Mama scammed the man.

536
00:23:37,749 --> 00:23:39,376
That's why he chased her.

537
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:42,963
The man said, Scammer, scammer!"

538
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:44,798
[pensive music playing]

539
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:47,259
I hope Mama is okay.

540
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:51,388
[tense music playing]

541
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,776
Oh, brother, hurry up!

542
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:05,694
Well…

543
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:08,071
Gosh, I told you,
run after her immediately!

544
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:09,614
- My God, she's a scammer!
- We're looking for her, sir.

545
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,158
Where is she? You're too slow.

546
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:13,326
We should've caught her already.

547
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:14,828
She's a thief!

548
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:20,083
- Nothing, sir.
- Oh no.

549
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,251
[sighs]

550
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:25,088
You're too slow! You need to find her.

551
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:27,340
- [man] If she gets away, that's it!
- [guard] Sir, just report it

552
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:29,134
- to the office, sir.
- [man] That will take too long!

553
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:30,468
[guard] It will be resolved, sir.

554
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:32,053
- [man] Oh, no. Jeez.
- [guard] Just file a report.

555
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:32,971
Jeez.

556
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:44,608
[thumps]

557
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:59,998
[romantic music playing]

558
00:25:01,124 --> 00:25:02,375
[thuds]

559
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:03,793
Are you okay?

560
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:05,420
Ah, because me, I'm fine.

561
00:25:05,503 --> 00:25:07,464
Even if you stay here forever, my love.

562
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:09,382
- What do you mean, "My love"?!
- [quirky sting]

563
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:10,967
Ouch, ouch.

564
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:12,510
- Come on.
- Where is it?

565
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:15,180
[sneaky music playing]

566
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:17,349
[Olga] Oh my God!

567
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:19,100
[Olga pants]

568
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:21,895
[in English] Oh. Ah, may I?

569
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:24,147
[Emerson] Ah.

570
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:27,108
Mmm.

571
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:28,568
[pleasant music playing]

572
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:29,903
[in English] Perfect fit, ah.

573
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:31,571
Like a fairytale.

574
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:33,240
- [chuckles]
- Of course, it's perfect!

575
00:25:33,323 --> 00:25:34,282
That's my shoe!

576
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:35,200
[grunts and groans]

577
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:36,743
- [thumps]
- [Olga, in English] Fool!

578
00:25:36,826 --> 00:25:39,037
- I'm just helping you.
- [guard] There's someone there.

579
00:25:39,871 --> 00:25:40,914
[Olga] I'm out of here!

580
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:43,708
[man, in English]
Maybe it's her! Stop her!

581
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:44,876
[Emerson, in English] My love!

582
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:47,212
[tense music playing]

583
00:25:48,463 --> 00:25:50,590
Wait. My love!

584
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:54,886
- [music fades]
- [electronic blipping]

585
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:58,932
[tense music playing]

586
00:26:02,477 --> 00:26:04,312
Oh? Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

587
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:06,106
The watch was immediately exposed as fake.

588
00:26:06,189 --> 00:26:07,357
I haven't even left yet.

589
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,901
What's important is you
and the money are safe.

590
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:11,736
I thought I could escape.

591
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:12,821
UP NEXT

592
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:14,614
[Olga] <i>That fool bumped into me.</i>

593
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:15,865
That was you.

594
00:26:15,949 --> 00:26:17,575
You just don't have your mole, but…

595
00:26:18,493 --> 00:26:20,537
I can't be mistaken.

596
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:21,955
[dramatic sting]

597
00:26:22,038 --> 00:26:23,581
Liar!

598
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:26,543
I'm your mother. You're my daughter!

599
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:29,337
What do you want me to do
so you'll believe me, Ibyang?

600
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,589
What are you saying?
I'm not a member of the syndicate.

601
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:33,800
<i>You're even doubting</i>
<i>your family now.</i>

602
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:35,218
<i>You're too paranoid.</i>

603
00:26:35,302 --> 00:26:36,761
[in English] Oh my God.

604
00:26:36,845 --> 00:26:39,639
[in English] Our intel told us
that the decoder of this town

605
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:40,724
is the mayor's niece.

606
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:42,267
[in English] <i>So, she might be here.</i>

607
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:43,518
[Samir, in English] <i>He might be here too.</i>

608
00:26:43,601 --> 00:26:45,854
[in English] This man has many faces.

609
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:49,024
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

610
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:50,692
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

611
00:26:50,775 --> 00:26:52,902
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

612
00:26:52,986 --> 00:26:56,114
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

613
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:58,325
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

614
00:26:58,408 --> 00:27:00,493
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
